Subject: Why do images flicker in production, and what can I do to fix it?
Message-ID: <rN80xtaEr5c.MCPl4fvsYZIJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shinyapps-users/c/rN80xtaEr5c/m/MCPl4fvsYZIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Here's a pretty simple shiny app:

server.R

library(shiny)

shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {
  vals = reactiveValues(counter=0)

  output$graph = renderPlot({
    plot(runif(100), runif(100), main=paste("Counter:", vals$counter))
  })

  loop = observe({
    for(i in 1:10000) {
      x = runif(100)
    }

    isolate({vals$counter = vals$counter + 1})

    if (isolate(vals$counter) < 100) {
      invalidateLater(0, session)
    }
  })
})

ui.R

shinyUI(fluidPage(
  plotOutput("graph")
))

I've hosted this at shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, here's the URL: https://todd.shinyapps.io/testing-plot-flicker/

Note that the counter in the title of the plot should increment by 1 every time the plot renders. However, if you watch the counter go, a lot of the time it will jump by 2, 3, or 4, I've even seen as high as 8 on occasion. Why aren't all of those plots getting rendered? Is there a way I can tell shiny to wait for the plot to be rendered on the client before re-executing the loop? I would be willing to increase total runtime in exchange for a guarantee that all plots will be rendered

Thanks,
Todd

