OL LQ,

Thank you for your input.

I see. I have some files that I read into my App, depending upon user's selection. I had saved these files in UTF-8 encoding. And I don't think they are causing the problem, as a simpler version of my App is able to read the files properly. Given this, I did inspect my code files to see if they had any strange characters, but they too did not... So I'm confused as to what the source of error is...

Yihui,

Thank you for your contribution.
My apologies, I had taken down my app to try to find the source of error, but forgot to upload it back.

This is the link to my app: https://kazmialiarsalan.shinyapps.io/QualitativeAnalysisApp-R_v8/
The Server <https://github.com/noobuseR/QualitativeAnalysisApp-R/blob/master/server.R> and UI <https://github.com/noobuseR/QualitativeAnalysisApp-R/blob/master/ui.R> files can be found at the links.
The text data sets that I am reading into my app can be found here <https://github.com/noobuseR/Datasets>.

An older, simpler version of my app that runs just fine can be found here <https://aliakazmi.shinyapps.io/QualitativeAnalysisApp-R/>. The difference between this and new app is that the older was constructed using older version of packages, and did not include the topicmodels package either. The older app was constructed a few months back.

Regarding the use of scan(textConnection()), I was using getURL() to read in raw text data from my GitHub, so once I had done
data<- getURL(...)
I couldn't use the readLines() function, and had to rely on a textConnection() first, after which scan() is possible.
I am amateurish with R :)

Thanks.

